html2wp Source-Available Licence
Version 1.0, 2026-08-22

Copyright (c) 2026 BELNEM s.r.o. All rights reserved.

This software is source-available, not open source.

Trying it, learning from it, and using it on things you are not paid for is
free and needs no key. Using it in a business — converting a site for a
client, or for a company you run — needs a current licence key. Taking it to
build your own conversion product is not permitted at all, and that holds
whether you write that product yourself or have an AI write it from this.


1. DEFINITIONS

   "the Software"    this skill: the SKILL.md instructions, the scripts under
                     assets/, and any documentation shipped with them.

   "the Service"     the hosted conversion service the Software calls, at
                     api.html2wp.dev or any successor address. The Service is
                     NOT part of the Software and is not licensed here; its
                     use is governed by its own terms, at
                     https://html2wp.dev/service-terms.html

   "Output"          the WordPress themes, content bundles, reports and other
                     files produced by running the Software. Your Output is
                     yours — see section 4.

   "Commercial Use"  using the Software in the course of a business, a trade,
                     a profession or any other undertaking, or for money or
                     other commercial advantage. Converting a website for a
                     client, for an employer, or for a business you own or
                     operate is Commercial Use — whether or not you invoice
                     the conversion itself as a separate line.

   "a Key"           a current html2wp licence key issued by the Licensor.
                     Its scope — the term, and how many conversions, sites or
                     people it covers — is whatever you were given when it was
                     issued. A later change to the published plans does not
                     narrow a Key already issued. Keys are at
                     https://html2wp.dev/licenses

   "Licensor"        BELNEM s.r.o., Beckovska 5, 821 04 Bratislava, Slovakia.
                     Company ID (ICO) 53713486, registered in the Commercial
                     Register of the Municipal Court Bratislava III, Section
                     Sro, Insert No. 152015/B.

   "you"             the person or organisation exercising rights under this
                     licence.


2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   Subject to section 3:

   a) WITHOUT A KEY — any use that is not Commercial Use.

      Evaluate the Software, run it against your own personal site, learn
      from it, take it apart to see how it works. The free tier of the
      Service exists for precisely this, and no fee is due for any of it.

      Teaching is included: show it, discuss it, run it in front of a class.
      Handing out copies is a different act and is governed by 3(a) — if a
      course needs that, ask, because the answer is usually yes.

   b) WITH A KEY — Commercial Use.

      While you hold a Key you may run the Software in your business and FOR
      CLIENTS, charge whatever you like for that work, and deliver the Output
      to them without restriction. Running an agency, a freelance practice or
      a studio on this Software is a supported and intended use; the agency
      licences exist for exactly that.

      If a Key lapses, the rights in this paragraph lapse with it. That is
      expiry, not breach, and section 4 keeps the Output you already have.

   c) modify the Software for your own use — fixing it, extending it, and
      adapting it to a project's needs — within whichever of 2a or 2b applies
      to that use;

   d) make copies as needed to do the above, within your own organisation.

   The Key is the only thing that separates 2a from 2b. Nothing else in this
   licence is conditional on holding one, and the Software is not crippled
   without one: a licence buys headroom and permission, never a better result.


3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   a) You may not distribute, publish, sublicense, sell or otherwise make the
      Software — or a modified version of it, or a substantial part of it —
      available to anyone outside your organisation.

      This does not restrict the ordinary business of running it. The Software
      travels through other people's systems every time you use it as
      intended, and that is fine: AI providers, whose assistants read and
      execute it; cloud, hosting and backup providers; and contractors or
      freelancers working on your behalf — each may hold and process it as far
      as a use permitted under section 2 requires.

   b) You may not put the CONVERSION TECHNOLOGY into anyone else's hands.

      That is: you may not use the Software, or anything derived from it, to
      build, offer or operate a service, a SaaS, an API, a plugin, a skill, a
      CLI, an agent, a platform or any other tool with which other people
      convert websites — nor anything that otherwise competes with the
      Software or the Service.

      The line runs between the work and the tool:

        permitted     you run the Software and hand your client the finished
                      theme. This is section 2b, and it is the point of the
                      product — an agency doing this all day is a customer,
                      not a competitor.

        not permitted you hand your client, or the public, something that
                      does the converting.

      This applies however the work is done: by a person who has read the
      Software, or by an AI system that you point at it.

   c) You may not use the Software as training data, as fine-tuning material,
      as retrieval or context material, or as any other input to a machine
      learning or AI system, where the purpose or the effect is to produce
      something that would breach paragraph (b) if you had written it
      yourself.

      This does NOT restrict the ordinary operation of the Software. The
      Software is written to be read and executed by an AI coding assistant —
      that is what it is for. An assistant reading SKILL.md, following it, and
      running the scripts to convert a site is the intended use, and is
      permitted under section 2 like any other way of running it.

   d) You may not use the Software as a means of studying, probing or
      reverse-engineering the Service in order to reproduce it.

   e) You may not remove, disable or circumvent the parts of the Software that
      identify a licence to the Service, report conversion results to it, or
      enforce its limits.

   f) You may not remove or alter this licence, the copyright notice, or the
      attribution in the files that carry it.

   Nothing in this section takes away a right that mandatory law gives a
   lawful user and that cannot be signed away — including, in the European
   Union, the right to observe, study and test how the Software works while
   running it, in order to work out the ideas and principles behind it. Those
   ideas are not claimed here; the expression is.


4. YOUR OUTPUT IS YOURS

   The Licensor claims no ownership of and asserts no rights over your Output.
   A theme this Software produces from your design is yours: you may use it,
   modify it, sell it, hand it to a client, or publish it, with no obligation
   to the Licensor and no obligation to mention the Software.

   This is unconditional. It does not depend on holding a Key, and it survives
   the termination of this licence under section 6 — a theme you converted
   stays yours whatever happens afterwards.

   Owning your Output settles nothing else. It is not a waiver of any claim
   the Licensor has for use of the Software that was unlicensed or otherwise
   prohibited: the themes stay yours, and the breach stays a breach.

   And this section gives you what the Licensor has to give, not more. It
   grants rights only in material the Licensor owns or may license. Fonts,
   images, icons, libraries, and any template your input was built on arrive
   with terms of their own; those terms are untouched by this licence and
   remain yours to honour. Nothing is cleared by passing through this
   Software — what went in encumbered comes out encumbered.

   The Output may include runtime code generated from the Licensor's templates.
   Section 4 grants you all rights necessary to use, modify and distribute that
   code as part of your Output, and only as part of your Output.


5. NO OTHER RIGHTS

   Rights not expressly granted are reserved. In particular this licence grants
   no trademark rights: "html2wp", "Visual Edit" and the Licensor's other marks
   remain the Licensor's, and this licence does not permit you to use them to
   name, brand or promote anything of yours.


6. TERMINATION

   This licence ends automatically if you breach section 3, or use the
   Software outside the scope of section 2 — commercial use without a Key
   being the case that matters — and do not cure it within 30 days of being
   notified.

   Curing unlicensed Commercial Use means obtaining the Key that use required.
   Cure does not retroactively licence past use, and does not waive a claim
   that has already accrued, unless the Licensor agrees otherwise in writing.

   In the ordinary case the Licensor will seek the purchase of the right Key
   rather than termination. Someone who did not realise a Key was needed
   should obtain one, and may then carry on using the Software.

   The paragraph above exists for the other case — two years of unlicensed
   commercial work is not settled by buying one Key at the end of it.

   On termination you must stop using the Software and destroy your copies.
   Section 4 survives: your Output remains yours.


